SUMMARY:Pre-Event Picnic - Olivette Riverside Concert  
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\n*What could be better than a Sunday aftern
 oon of connecting\, socializing\, and listening to great music with fellow
  Nomads at an outdoor concert by the beautiful French Broad River?*\n\n**W
 hat:** Pre-Concert Social\n**Where:** The Lawn - Olivette Riverside Pavili
 on\n**Artists:** GOLDPINE\n**When:** 3pm on Sunday\, April 19th\n**To Brin
 g:** BYOB & BYOC (chair) + sharable food\n\n**Details**\nJoin fellow music
 -loving Nomads for a pre-concert picnic on the lawn by the Olivette Rivers
 ide Pavilion. Use [this link](https://www.chatthillsmusic.com/goldpine) to
  purchase tickets to the GOLDPINE concert on Sunday\, April 19th. Nomads a
 ttending the concert are invited to bring shareable snacks and appetizers\
 , along with your beverages of choice.\n\nThis informal Nomads gathering s
 tarts at 3pm. Live music from GOLDPINE will be from 4 - 6pm.\n\nBring comf
 ortable folding chairs and/or blankets for picnicking on the lawn. It you 
 want to sit in the Pavilion for the concert\, you will need your own chair
 .\n\n**The Music**\nChatt Hills welcomes GOLDPINE for the first event in t
 heir 2026 "[Sundays by the River](https://www.chatthillsmusic.com/all-show
 s)" concert series. Fans of contemporary Americana will love this folksy a
 nd energetic husband-wife duo. Pairing award-winning songwriting with stro
 ng vocals and harmony\, Nashville-based GOLDPINE presents engaging stories
  about life\, love and the human experience.\nTo sample what is in store f
 rom Ben and Kassie\, check out [this video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?
 v=Hri3PoSysDM).\n\n**Tickets**\nWe highly recommend purchasing your ticket
 s in advance. Tickets are $25 each ($30.52\, including fees) -- and kids a
 re free! Well-behaved dogs are also welcome.\n\n[Tickets and more info](ht
 tps://www.chatthillsmusic.com/goldpine).\n\n**Directions**\nOlivette is ju
 st 15 minutes from downtown Asheville. Click [this link](https://maps.app.
 goo.gl/rnqGwUiLLJghxo1r8) to get directions directly to the parking area f
 or the Pavilion. Otherwise\, use the address below to get to Olivette and 
 follow the Chatt Hills event signs to the Pavilion.\nCarpooling is encoura
 ged.\n\n**Chatt Hills Music**\nChatt Hills Music is an independent non-pro
 fit organization dedicated to enriching communities through the power of l
 ive music. Chatt Hills brings an eclectic lineup of award-winning artists 
 to Asheville and the surrounding region. From Americana and singer-songwri
 ters to jazz\, rock\, and classical\, every concert offers a unique musica
 l experience.\nThis outdoor concert series takes place just minutes from d
 owntown Asheville at the scenic Olivette Riverside Pavilion\, located alon
 g the banks of the French Broad River—where great music meets beautiful 
 views.\nWorld-class music\, scenic views\, affordable tickets — and kids
  are always free.\n\n**The Venue**\nOlivette is a 411-acre planned communi
 ty and historic farm\, located along the French Broad River\, just 6.7 mil
 es from downtown Asheville. An agrihood community\, Olivette is home to a 
 vibrant vegetable\, fruit and flower farm. With 1.3 miles of river frontag
 e\, the community has a seven acre riverfront park with a pavilion\, miles
  of walking trails\, community gardens\, a dog park\, and multiple neighbo
 rhood gathering spaces.
