SUMMARY:Coworking day: Bankers Hours in Marshall
DESCRIPTION:AVL Digital Nomads\nJoin us for a focused and relaxed coworkin
 g day at Bankers Hours\, a beautifully restored historic space in the hear
 t of Marshall\, North Carolina.\n\nNestled in a quiet mountain town just o
 utside Asheville\, Marshall offers a refreshing change of pace—think wal
 kable streets\, charming cafes\, and a peaceful riverside atmosphere that 
 makes it easy to settle into deep work. Bankers Hours itself carries that 
 same energy\, blending old-world character with a warm\, functional worksp
 ace that feels both inspiring and unpretentious.\n\nWe’ll gather from 9:
 00 AM to 5:00 PM on April 21 for a full day of independent work alongside 
 a small group of like-minded professionals. With attendance capped at 15 p
 eople\, the environment stays focused\, comfortable\, and conducive to rea
 l productivity.\n\nIf the weather cooperates\, we’ll have access to the 
 rooftop patio—a quiet favorite for reading\, thinking\, or getting some 
 sun while you work. It’s one of those rare spots that makes you want to 
 slow down just enough to do your best thinking.\nMarshall has several near
 by restaurants and cafes within easy walking distance\, making lunch break
 s simple and enjoyable.\n\nParking note: The bank lot may fill up\, but ad
 ditional public parking is available throughout town just a short walk awa
 y.\nWhether you’re looking to make progress on a big project or just wan
 t a change of scenery\, this coworking day offers a calm\, intentional set
 ting to get things done.\n\nWe might just take a walk to a brewery down th
 e street at 4pm!
